# kvd's demo: two clients, A and B, of one server on the loopback; the
# server's clock is manual and moves only at an @clock line.
== strings
A> PING
A> SET greeting "hello, world"
A> GET greeting
B> APPEND greeting "!"
A> GET greeting
A> SET greeting "bonjour" XX GET
A> SET greeting "hi" NX
A> INCR visits
A> INCRBY visits 41
A> INCR greeting
A> MSET colour red size L
A> MGET colour size nothing
A> GETRANGE greeting 0 2
@pipeline B
SET page:1 "the first page"
INCR hits
INCR hits
GET page:1
DEL page:1 nothing
@end

== lists, hashes, sets and sorted sets
A> RPUSH queue job1 job2 job3
A> LPUSH queue job0
A> LPOP queue
A> LRANGE queue 0 -1
A> HSET user:1 name Ada born 1815 field "analytical engine"
A> HGET user:1 name
A> HINCRBY user:1 born 1
A> HGETALL user:1
A> SADD tags redis heroes kv heroes
A> SADD other kv rust
A> SINTER tags other
A> SISMEMBER tags heroes
A> ZADD board 120 ada 95 bob 133 cyd 120 abe
A> ZRANGE board 0 -1 WITHSCORES
A> ZREVRANK board ada
A> ZINCRBY board 40 bob
A> ZRANGEBYSCORE board (120 +inf WITHSCORES
A> ZCOUNT board -inf 120
A> TYPE board
A> LPUSH board oops

== keys that expire
A> SET session abc PX 1500
A> SET token xyz EX 2
A> SET flag on EX 1
A> PTTL session
A> TTL token
@clock 1600
A> GET session
A> TTL token
@clock 1000
A> DBSIZE
A> INFO keyspace

== publish and subscribe
A> SUBSCRIBE news
B> PUBLISH news "kvd 0.1 is out"
A<
B> PUBLISH sport "nobody listens"
A> PSUBSCRIBE n*
B> PUBLISH news again
A<
A<
A> UNSUBSCRIBE
A> PUNSUBSCRIBE

== a transaction WATCH aborts, and the same transaction again
A> SET balance 100
A> WATCH balance
A> GET balance
B> INCRBY balance 50
A> MULTI
A> DECRBY balance 30
A> RPUSH ledger "-30"
A> EXEC
A> WATCH balance
A> GET balance
A> MULTI
A> DECRBY balance 30
A> RPUSH ledger "-30"
A> EXEC
A> MULTI
A> SET x 1
A> NOSUCHCOMMAND
A> EXEC

== scanning the keys
A> SCAN 0 MATCH user:* COUNT 100
A> SCAN 0 TYPE zset COUNT 100
A> KEYS b*

== a snapshot, a background one, and a restart that replays the log
A> SAVE
A> SET after-save 1
A> RPUSH queue job4
@files
A> BGSAVE
A> SET after-bgsave 2
@restart
A> GET after-save
A> GET after-bgsave
A> LRANGE queue 0 -1
A> ZRANGE board 0 -1 WITHSCORES
A> GET balance
A> INFO persistence

== a crash in the middle of a write
A> SET last-words "written whole"
@crash
A> GET last-words
A> GET lost
A> DBSIZE
A> INFO stats
